        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Oneworld, Finnair, US Airways, Finnish Aviation Academy\n- Places: Finland, Vantaa, Helsinki Airport, Pori\n- Topics: airline alliances, airline ownership, flag carriers\n\nFacts:\n- Oneworld is an airline alliance founded on 1 February 1999.\n- Finnair is the flag carrier and largest airline of Finland, and its headquarters are in Vantaa on the grounds of Helsinki Airport, which is its main hub.\n- In March 2014, US Airways became an affiliate member of Oneworld after previously being a member of Star Alliance.\n- Finnish Aviation Academy is a private school owned by the state of Finland, Finnair, and the city of Pori.",
